IO-55: book off-curve pump time as Low or High by the side of the curve

pump_getInflow() marked a Type1, Type2, Type3 or Type5 pump that operates
outside its curve with Link.flowClass = YES. YES is 1, which is UP_DRY in
the flow-class enumeration, and stats_updateLinkStats() counts UP_DRY as
"High" and DN_DRY as "Low", so all off-curve time of these pumps went to
the High column, including time spent below the curve's first point. Set
DN_DRY below the curve and UP_DRY above it, as the Type4 case already does.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-55_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/link.c b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
index 31925e1..cd55ba4 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/link.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
@@ -1583,8 +1583,8 @@ double pump_getInflow(int j)
         qIn = table_intervalLookup(&Curve[m], vol) / UCF(FLOW);
 
         // --- check if off of pump curve
-        if ( vol < Pump[k].xMin || vol > Pump[k].xMax )
-            Link[j].flowClass = YES;
+        if ( vol < Pump[k].xMin ) Link[j].flowClass = DN_DRY;
+        if ( vol > Pump[k].xMax ) Link[j].flowClass = UP_DRY;
         break;
 
       case PUMP2_CURVE:
@@ -1592,8 +1592,8 @@ double pump_getInflow(int j)
         qIn = table_intervalLookup(&Curve[m], depth) / UCF(FLOW);
 
         // --- check if off of pump curve
-        if ( depth < Pump[k].xMin || depth > Pump[k].xMax )
-            Link[j].flowClass = YES;
+        if ( depth < Pump[k].xMin ) Link[j].flowClass = DN_DRY;
+        if ( depth > Pump[k].xMax ) Link[j].flowClass = UP_DRY;
         break;
 
       case PUMP3_CURVE:
@@ -1610,8 +1610,8 @@ double pump_getInflow(int j)
               UCF(LENGTH) / UCF(FLOW) / s;
 
           // --- check if off of pump curve
-          if (head < Pump[k].xMin || head > Pump[k].xMax)
-              Link[j].flowClass = YES;
+          if (head < Pump[k].xMin) Link[j].flowClass = DN_DRY;
+          if (head > Pump[k].xMax) Link[j].flowClass = UP_DRY;
           break;
 
       case PUMP4_CURVE:
